S=['# Unwelded 2hb_1xT: all retained runs, November 10, 2026','', 'Read-only analysis. No dynamics launched, force fields changed, or molecular structures authored.','', '## Coverage and methods','',f"Analyzed all 13 matching jobs: nine production jobs and four preparation histories. Production contains {sum(r['frames'] for r in R):,} unique saved frames, representing approximately {sum(r['sampled_exposure_ns'] for r in R):.2f} ns of sampled exposure across nonidentical protocols. This is not one continuous trajectory or an equilibrium ensemble. Every native saved frame was screened for all 153 thymine pairs. Production and restrained preparation remain separate.",'','The intended ordered endpoints are D001:15 then D000:8. Classifier identities I/II depend on endpoint order. The geometric screen assumes retained-neighbor suprafacial approach; it does not model excitation, quantum yields, reaction barriers, photoreversal, or isomer interconversion. Primary thresholds: both proposed bond distances 2.5–4.0 Å, absolute mapped torsion ≤45°, all four approach-face stereochemical signs matching, minimum normal-approach margin ≥0.25. Sensitivity grid: distance 3.6/4.0/4.5 Å × torsion 30/45/60° × margin 0.1/0.25/0.5. Catalog coverage does not establish chemical formation admissibility of every registered product.','','Periodic images are reconstructed locally before contact measurements. Pairing is a distance proxy: all reference hydrogen-bond distances for a designed pair must remain within reference +0.75 Å. Local pairing covers designed pairs containing an endpoint-neighbor residue (±1); it is not a hydrogen-bond angle criterion or a melting measurement. Samples are correlated; occupancies below are descriptive time fractions, not independent observations or product probabilities.','','## Production results','','| Created (Denver) / ID | Retained time (ns) | Frames | Mean intended midpoint (Å) | Whole / local paired fraction | Primary intended frames | Distance-only frames ≤4 Å |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
